# Testing Standards

## Layout

- `tests/unit/` — fast, isolated (config, parsers, agents with mocks).
- `tests/integration/` — SQLite, vector store, multi-module.
- `tests/e2e/` — full `research` CLI flows (mark `@pytest.mark.e2e` when added).

## Practices

```python
# ✅ Isolate filesystem — never touch ~/.research-agent in tests
@pytest.fixture
def config_dir(tmp_path: Path) -> Path:
    return tmp_path / "research-agent"

cfg = Config.load(config_dir)
```

- Mock LLM at `LLMClient` boundary; inject fakes, do not call DeepSeek in unit tests.
- CLI tests: `typer.testing.CliRunner` + `monkeypatch` on `_load_config` for temp dirs.
- One behavior per test; descriptive names: `test_masked_api_key_redacts_long_key`.

## Commands

```bash
pytest
pytest tests/unit -v
ruff check src tests && mypy src
```
